<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Arches-Charleville</h1><p class="st-meta">1606 CE – 1708 CE · capital Charleville</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A sovereign principality on the Meuse where Charles of Gonzaga founded the planned city of Charleville in 1606.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-duke-of-mantua">Charles of Gonzaga</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-nevers">Nevers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rethel">Rethel</a>, held the land of Arches on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>, which claimed to lie outside both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Empire. In 1606 he founded a new town there, Charleville, named after himself, and ruled it as a sovereign principality.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Charleville was laid out on a regular plan around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/place-ducale">Place Ducale</a>, modelled on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/place-des-vosges">Place des Vosges</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. The principality minted its own coins and attracted craftsmen with tax exemptions. Charles later became duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Mantua</a> in 1627, and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> heirs ruled the principality from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> duke, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-carlo-gonzaga">Ferdinando Carlo</a>, died in 1708 after siding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> then took the principality into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>, though the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon-conde">Condé family</a> claimed it.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1606 CE – 1708 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.66%;width:2.03%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1606 CE – 1708 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Charleville</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles I Gonzaga, Ferdinando Carlo Gonzaga</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Charleville</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1657&amp;focus=principality-of-arches-charleville" aria-label="Principality of Arches-Charleville on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4765 473 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Arches-Charleville lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5085 729L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5085 729h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5085 729h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Charleville. <a href="/atlas?year=1657&amp;focus=principality-of-arches-charleville">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
